# wiki-interest

- Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before changing resolve, pageviews, metrics, charts, or the PDF.
- The model interprets requests and explains `analysis.json`. Python calculates every number.
- Do not invent Wikipedia titles, pageview rows, or metric values in code, docs, or tests.
- Do not add Wikidata, caches, thresholds, extra CLI commands, or an automated model runner.
- Keep business rules in one module. Do not copy metric formulas into `SKILL.md`.
- Unit tests must not call the network. Use fixtures for HTTP later.
- Run `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v` with `PYTHONPATH=src` after a code change.
- Do not expand the milestone in progress unless the task says to.
